# Catching spaceships at the edge of the grid, with the border closed and open. Expects the
# default start-up (single rotation, 256×256).
wait 25; clear

# The list can be looked at before anything is caught; ticking the box opens it as well.
key s; wait 20; expect_text CatcherNote Catching is off.
key s; wait 3

# The lightest ship, heading for the right edge, and a diagonal one heading for the corner.
place $2o2$2o 240 120
place 3o$o$bo 236 236
click Catching; wait 20; expect_checked Catching on; expect_checked CatcherCatching on
expect_text CatcherNote No spaceships yet: let a blob run.
shot catcher-1-armed

# The first ship has 14 cells to go at a cell per 6 generations; the other takes longer. The
# border is closed, and still they are taken out where they would have wrapped around.
step 120; wait 10; expect_caught 1 1; expect_population 5
step 400; wait 20; expect_caught 2 2; expect_population 0
expect_text CatcherNote Click a pattern to pick it up, or shift-click it to copy it as text.
shot catcher-2-two-kinds

# Without catching, a closed border lets a ship come round again and an open one lets it
# leave; neither counts it.
key k; wait 3; expect_checked Catching off
place $2o2$2o 240 120
step 120; expect_population 4
key o; wait 3; expect_checked OpenBorder on
step 1600; wait 10; expect_population 0; expect_caught 2 2

# A blob, left to evaporate through the open border. The rows stay put while the list grows,
# so a click lands also while the catches come in: with shift, it copies the pattern as text.
key k; wait 3
blob; speed 240; stride 32; play; wait 200
press Shift; click Kind0; release Shift; wait 3; expect_clipboard b2o2$b2o
wait 200; pause; wait 20
shot catcher-3-haul

# A click picks the pattern up; a click on the grid puts it down, on the blocks of the current
# partition, so that it flies: the lightest ship, two cells to the right every 12 generations.
clear; wait 2; expect_population 0
click Kind0; wait 3
expect_text CatcherNote Click the grid to put the pattern down, as often as you like. Escape or a right click lets go of it.
move Grid 0 0; wait 3; shot catcher-4-ghost
click Grid 0 0; wait 3; expect_population 4
expect_cell 127 126 on; expect_cell 128 128 on
step 120; wait 2; expect_population 4; expect_cell 147 126 on; expect_cell 148 128 on
# It stays picked up until Escape; a click on its row would let go of it as well.
click Grid -100 60; wait 3; expect_population 8
key Escape; wait 3; expect_text CatcherNote Click a pattern to pick it up, or shift-click it to copy it as text.
click Grid 100 -60; wait 3; expect_population 9

# A slow spaceship: a loose cloud of five to seven cells that is back in its shape after
# 13 774 generations, four cells on along the diagonal. It leaves whole, and is known for
# what it is once it has been followed for long enough, which another thread does.
rule 15,7,6,3,11,12,4,8,14,13,5,9,10,2,1,0; clear; wait 3
place 4bo$3bo2$5bobo2$bo2$5bobo 236 222
step 60000; wait 3; expect_population 0
until expect_caught 1 1
shot catcher-5-slow
rule single-rotation; wait 3

# Forgetting empties the list of this rule; the key closes the panel.
click CatcherForget; wait 20; expect_caught 0 0
key s; wait 4; shot catcher-6-closed
quit
